only on CBS this morning we are  revealing the winners of national  Geographics 2018 Travel Photographer of  the Year contest National Geographic  received more than 13,000 entries from  professional and amateur photographers  around the world the annual contest is  divided into three categories nature  cities and people the grand prize and  nature category winner is underwater  photographer Reiko takahashi wow look at  that  her photo is called mermaid and it shows  the tail of a humpback whale calf off  the Japanese coast a Swiss photographer  won the people category with this photo  capturing Mongolian hospitality titled  tea culture and this photo taken from  the inside of a tram in Nagasaki Japan  won the cities category the runners-up  include an aerial perspective of a  pyramid at this Mexican archeological  site these haitian twin sisters playing  in front of their home in Brazil and  flamingos taking off from a lake in  Tanzania you can see more of national  Geographics winning photos on our CBS  this morning Instagram page I always  loved that competition you see some  suitable things gorgeous
 

